codex
**REVISE — T241’s layered SVG is the right construction. The Plan’s default schedule and promised swaps violate its own state boundaries.**

1. **Convergent freeze — closed by construction.** T15 attempt 1’s motion and reusability lenses scored 68 and 64 and independently identified the frozen surplus. T241 draws a static population array and animates separate SVG layers. No element is borrowed from a moving pool, so the reserve and velocity-continuity failure cannot occur. The array-only hold is an intentional state. [T15 scores, Attempt 1](../../../../study/recreations/T15-particle-typography/scores.md) · [T241 Plan §§2.2–2.3](item-T241-observe-plan.md#22-census-anchor-mapping-a102--departure-table)

2. **Owner catches — layer roles are explicit, but sequencing is underspecified.** The `ink`/`dim`/`faint` assignments establish the default hierarchy. Keep the array and selection ring in the persistent group, and validate that supported palette swaps preserve the hierarchy. For sequencing, distinguish ordered entrances with intentional overlap from exclusive active beats. The default array finishes at `600 + 39 × 14 + 180 = 1326 ms`, so only 16 icons are fully drawn at the 1000 ms checkpoint that claims all 40. The promised timing swap ends expansion at `1400 + 2 × (1000 + 50) + 1000 = 4500 ms`, after slot fill starts at 3500 ms and after the board is declared complete at 3900 ms. Correct the checkpoint and derive dependent beat starts from prior completions. Preserve the default slot anchor and let the swap move it when necessary. Assert that the hold follows both expansion and slot fill, and that dissolve follows the hold. Gate fills, labels, and markers at entry as well as strokes. Dash offset alone cannot enforce their visibility. [T241 Plan §§2.1–2.5](item-T241-observe-plan.md#21-parameter-table-every-variable--a-config-key-specimen-value--default) · [INSTRUCTION A5](../../INSTRUCTION.md#amendment-a5-2026-11-14--the-owners-own-read-on-t15-attempt-1--two-cures--the-fifth-lens)

3. **Parameterization — separate specimen facts from runtime rules.** The default’s `4 × 10 = 40` is a specimen assertion. Applying that assertion to the promised `4 × 8 = 32` swap would halt a valid configuration. Check the specimen count on the default and assert `renderedCount === rows × cols` plus a valid selected index on every config. Derive the ring and connector endpoints from that index and the grid geometry. Bind the condition slot to the formula layout, and give the reticle pulse and dim cue explicit timing or record their simplification. The content swap also leaves expansion line 3 reporting `P(F | H) = 0.9811` under a `P(S|R) ≈ 0.87` headline. Swap the dependent result with the formula and test the resulting claim as a unit. [T241 Observe §§1.1, 1.4 and Plan §§2.1, 2.4–2.5](item-T241-observe-plan.md)

4. **Predicted minimum — timing/tempo.** T241/T242/T243 have no filed family scores, so this is a fleet-based risk prediction. The Plan deliberately substitutes a 1400 ms build for an already-standing opening and delays the first expansion line. It also dims the reticle at 3900 ms against the observed cue around 5000 ms. The five scores must total at least 425, and a minimum of 70 would require the other four to average 88.75. Readability is the next risk. The fit plan calls for shrinking to cure overflow and enlarging to cure legibility, without defining a layout that can satisfy both. Specify bounded wrapping or reflow, a phone-size font floor, and a failure result if the text cannot fit within both bounds. [T241 Observe §§1.2, 1.5 and Plan §§2.2, 2.5](item-T241-observe-plan.md) · [INSTRUCTION §§2.3, 5](../../INSTRUCTION.md#2--plan)

5. **Size discipline — clear.** The board, formula reveal, and dissolve to the selected population array are the core mechanic. The bars are explicitly deferred to T242. For comparison playback, define a shared 13,000 ms endpoint and account for the extra 500 ms in the evidence cut. [RUN.md §1–§2](RUN.md) · [T241 scope and Plan §§2.2, 2.6](item-T241-observe-plan.md) · [INSTRUCTION §8](../../INSTRUCTION.md#8--size-discipline)

**Limits —** The proposed geometry, playback, and phone readability are unverified. **CANNOT READ** `T241-probability-board-opening/build-record.md` — No such file or directory. The construction verdict is based on the on-disk Phase A record and wave Plan.

